# Binary assets must NEVER go through end-of-line conversion.
#
# Git guesses text-vs-binary by looking for a NUL byte in the first 8 KB.
# Some PDFs (uncompressed content streams) and some audio files have no NUL
# up there, so git calls them text - and on Windows, where core.autocrlf is
# true, every checkout then rewrites their LF bytes to CRLF and the file is
# corrupt. docs/fynewynz_wine_list.pdf committed exactly that way
# ("LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it").
#
# Marking the extensions explicitly is the only reliable fix: it turns the
# heuristic off for the file types where a wrong guess destroys data.
*.pdf   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.flac  binary
*.m4a   binary
*.aac   binary
*.opus  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.npy   binary
*.npz   binary
